  "result": "Excellent! All 199 tests pass (16 new statement tests added). Here's what I implemented:\n\n**Created src/statements.js** with the `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function that:\n- Validates the customer exists (returns CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND if not)\n- Filters invoices to only those for that customer with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n- Includes only invoices with issueDate on or before asOf (date-based cutoff)\n- Sorts results by issueDate\n- Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })` where each invoice has:\n  - `number`: invoice number\n  - `issueDate`: issue date\n  - `dueDate`: payment due date\n  - `total`: invoice total\n  - `due`: amount still owed (from `balanceDue`)\n- `totalDue` is the sum of all `due` amounts\n\n**Created test/statements.test.js** with 16 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Basic statement generation\n- Due amount calculations with partial payments\n- Date filtering (before, on, after cutoff dates)\n- Status filtering (excludes draft/paid, includes issued/partially_paid)\n- Invoice sorting by issueDate\n- Total due calculation\n- Customer ID normalization with whitespace/case\n- Error handling for unknown customers\n- Empty results for customers with no invoices\n- Multi-customer filtering\n- dueDate inclusion\n\nAll 199 tests pass successfully.",
